Student Email Agent

A web app that processes emails for students using AI. The app can extract content, categorize emails, and generate polite auto-replies. It consists of a FastAPI backend and a React frontend.

Features: 
- Extract sender, subject, urgency, deadlines, required actions, and a short summary from emails.

- Categorize emails into predefined categories:
 1. Class/Assignment
 2. Exam/Quiz/Deadlines
 3. Group Project/Collaboration
 4. Advising/Scheduling/Office Hours
 5. Spam/Low Priority
 6. Other

- Generates a professional, polite auto-reply for emails.
- Allows users to interact with the app in realtime through the Reach frontend. 

Prerequistes:
 - Python 3.10+
 - Node.js and npm
 - OpenAI API key

Dependencies:
 Backend: 
 - fastapi
 - uvicorn
 - python-dotenv
 - openai
 you can just run this to get everything installed: pip install fastapi uvicorn python-dotenv openai
 Frontend:
 - react should install everything automatically, so you should be good!

Instructions to get backend up:
 1. activate your virtual envornomnent each time you get started in your terminal
    - .\venv\Scripts\activate
 2. Navigate to the backend folder once you have the virtual environment up. Then run Uvicorn, if not installed install it.
    - cd backend
    - uvicorn main:app --reload
    If uvicorn is not installed, install it using: pip install uvicorn
 3. Terminal should then provide a link to test to see if the backend is running. However React's frontend already shows this. 
    - http://127.0.0.1:8000

Instructions for frontend set up: 
 1. Navigate to my-app (frontend) in a different terminal from the one used for backend
    - cd my-app
 2. Start up react
    - npm start
 If react is not installed run: npm install
 3. To check to see if the app is running, the terminal should show something like:
    - Local: http://localhost:3000 (should be the same)
    - On Your Network: http://192.168.1.XX:3000 (varies)

How to use:
 1. Open the frontend in your browser
    - http://localhost:3000
 2. Paste the email content into the text box
 3. Click the "Process Email" button
 4. Thats all you have to do!

Some notes to keep in mind:
    - You must have the frontend and backend running at the same time for the app to work
    - Create a .env file in the backend folder formatted like this:
         OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here
    - Make sure your OpenAI API key is in the .env file in the backend folder. I will not be using my personal key because it is sensitive information. 
    - The backend is made to log information for debugging, so if you have a hard time getting set up, check the logs